1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,329
[Characters, places and incidents
in this production]

2
00:00:03,329 --> 00:00:06,697
[are entirely fictitious.]

3
00:00:06,697 --> 00:00:10,023
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:01,094
<i>If Ran hadn't told me you were gay,</i>

5
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:03,440
<i>I would've thought you
had feelings for my sister</i>

6
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:05,638
<i>since you're this caring.</i>

7
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,547
<i>You don't have time to find a rich man, do you?</i>

8
00:01:08,547 --> 00:01:09,742
<i>Now that I'm rich,</i>

9
00:01:09,742 --> 00:01:11,167
<i>are you interested?</i>

10
00:01:11,167 --> 00:01:12,727
<i>No, thank you.</i>

11
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:16,121
<i>Don't you dare do what I think you'll do.</i>

12
00:01:16,121 --> 00:01:17,887
<i>You still love Daran, don't you?</i>

13
00:01:17,887 --> 00:01:19,280
<i>But you won't admit it,</i>

14
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,900
<i>so you put her outside your room.</i>

15
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:22,840
<i>If you were truly indifferent toward her,</i>

16
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:24,500
<i>you wouldn't be doing all of this.</i>

17
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,320
<i>The props we kept here
for our TV shows are gone.</i>

18
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:29,140
<i>They looked like... Daran.</i>

19
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:35,640
Someone reported that Sahaphet's props
in this studio are missing.

20
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,160
Did you steal them?

21
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:39,120
I didn't do it.

22
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:48,306
Don't give me that look.

23
00:01:48,306 --> 00:01:52,400
Yai gave you a chance,
and you still dared to steal from his company!

24
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:55,085
I said, I didn't do it.

25
00:01:55,085 --> 00:01:58,840
Yai, do you see now that she's the thief?

26
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:02,800
Why would you still keep her here?
Just fire her!

27
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,440
If there is evidence,

28
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:07,280
you can fire me or sue me, whatever you want.

29
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:09,144
But without evidence,

30
00:02:09,144 --> 00:02:13,080
you can't hit me
or baselessly accuse me like this.

31
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:21,680
Don't use violence here, Nana.

32
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:25,680
Without evidence, I can't fire anyone.

33
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:28,051
I have to follow the company's rules.

34
00:02:41,023 --> 00:02:43,600
Mr. Alex! Wake up! Something bad is happening!

35
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:45,760
Boy, I just got to sleep this morning!

36
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,298
Oh, come on!

37
00:02:47,298 --> 00:02:48,540
Are you going to get up?

38
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:50,760
Your angel is in big trouble!

39
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:53,040
- Huh?
- That's right!

40
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,400
I still believe you didn't do it,

41
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:58,190
because no one can be bad in every way.
Am I right?

42
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:02,455
It's up to you to decide.

43
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:06,307
Why are you protecting her, Yai?

44
00:03:06,307 --> 00:03:08,520
It's obvious she's the thief.

45
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,185
You don't have evidence, Nana.

46
00:03:10,185 --> 00:03:11,730
Why do you need so much evidence?

47
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:14,240
The security guard already
confirmed that it was her!

48
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:19,640
Yes, I saw with my own eyes
that Daran stole them.

49
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,765
Didn't you say she looked like Daran?

50
00:03:21,765 --> 00:03:23,680
Well, it's clear now.

51
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:26,580
Oh, wow.

52
00:03:28,568 --> 00:03:30,033
Excuse me,

53
00:03:30,033 --> 00:03:31,558
are you guys...

54
00:03:31,558 --> 00:03:35,000
acting in a vertical detective drama?

55
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:41,040
Like... there are witnesses,
testimonies, and all that.

56
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:44,600
If we go by the script,
those who make the biggest scene

57
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,000
end up embarrassed later.

58
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,880
Sam, why are you here?

59
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:50,360
Stop playing around and go.

60
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,199
I went to bed at 9 P.M.

61
00:03:52,199 --> 00:03:56,120
Whatever was stolen,
I had nothing to do with it.

62
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,156
There.

63
00:03:57,156 --> 00:03:59,280
That's the explanation we wanted.

64
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,425
Watch your mouth.

65
00:04:00,425 --> 00:04:02,450
You can't just claim that without evidence!

66
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:04,290
The evidence is here!

67
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,200
Lek.

68
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:12,280
I know everything now.

69
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:14,960
If anyone's going to accuse Ran of stealing,

70
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:18,705
I was with her all night.

71
00:04:18,705 --> 00:04:20,360
Lek.

72
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:22,840
Even you shouldn't just say things like that.

73
00:04:24,124 --> 00:04:27,145
Why are you here? Go back. You could get fired.

74
00:04:27,145 --> 00:04:29,460
I wasn't just saying things.

75
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:32,595
I can show you the CCTV footage if you want.

76
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:35,960
but...

77
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:38,920
the CCTV cameras in the studio
aren't working, Mr. Lek.

78
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:43,600
Even if those aren't working,
the one outside Ran's room is.

79
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,520
Let's watch it.

80
00:05:01,499 --> 00:05:02,960
So?

81
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:05,960
Are you saying that
just because she got into her room,

82
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,440
she couldn't be the thief?

83
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,760
If she could get in there,
then she could get out.

84
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:13,000
Stop being dramatic and watch the whole thing.

85
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:16,880
Ran got into her room at 8 P.M.

86
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:19,880
After that, she didn't leave the room at all.

87
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:22,340
Watch this.

88
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:36,032
Lek.

89
00:05:36,032 --> 00:05:37,960
Why did you get in there?

90
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,304
That's my room.

91
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:45,960
Ran and I share the same room.

92
00:05:52,399 --> 00:05:56,720
Since I was the one
who stayed with her all night,

93
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:00,429
would anyone still
accuse her of being the thief?

94
00:06:07,842 --> 00:06:12,467
Since the chairman's younger brother
has confirmed her alibi,

95
00:06:14,204 --> 00:06:16,440
we should put this matter to rest.

96
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:22,720
Come on.

97
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:25,760
Let's get away from here. Let's go.

98
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,619
Let's go, guys.

99
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:42,955
Yai, things were really stolen!

100
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:45,482
Stop bothering Daran already.

101
00:06:45,482 --> 00:06:47,720
Can you promise me, then,

102
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:50,353
that you'll also leave her alone?

103
00:06:50,353 --> 00:06:51,360
Listen to me.

104
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:57,240
The way you falsely accuse people
doesn't make me feel sorry for you at all.

105
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:59,888
It just makes me even less able to love you.

106
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:03,480
Yai...

107
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:06,408
You harassed an MJTV employee.

108
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:11,000
You should be grateful I didn't pull
your shows or cancel the series production.

109
00:07:15,948 --> 00:07:18,939
You're putting her before me.

110
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:24,280
How can I not think
that you still have feelings for her?

111
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,410
I don't need to answer that.

112
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:31,680
Fine.

113
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:34,680
I'll leave her alone.

114
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:38,080
But you still remember what I said, right?

115
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:41,240
If not, I'll remind you

116
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:45,380
I won't back down as easily as before.

117
00:08:07,201 --> 00:08:08,876
Lek.

118
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,200
Let's talk first.

119
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:17,120
I can let you play security guard,
but I can't let you live with Daran.

120
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:20,720
Do you know what you've done?

121
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:23,560
What are you concerned about?

122
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:25,360
Have you seen yourself?

123
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:28,320
Are you this angry because... you're jealous

124
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:30,560
- that I'm with Ran--
- Lek!

125
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:35,240
You can't let Daran live with you.

126
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:36,920
I can.

127
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:41,200
If you kick her out, get through me first.

128
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:18,680
Thanks for bringing me out here.

129
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:21,960
Good thing Mr. Alex came to save you in time.

130
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,080
But...

131
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:27,240
why are you...

132
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,810
sharing a room with Mr. Alex?

133
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:30,971
It couldn't be...

134
00:09:30,971 --> 00:09:33,184
Well, he's gay.

135
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:39,200
Right. Mr. Alex is gay.

136
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:41,000
That's right.

137
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:45,717
Hey.

138
00:09:45,717 --> 00:09:47,597
I'm fine.

139
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:56,862
Does your face still hurt? Let me see.

140
00:09:57,523 --> 00:09:59,203
No.

141
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:04,000
You're patient,

142
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,160
strong,

143
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:08,680
honest, and not afraid to speak the truth.

144
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:10,320
In the end,

145
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:12,920
the one who came after you ended up losing.

146
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,529
See?

147
00:10:24,347 --> 00:10:26,482
Do you want to come live with me?

148
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:30,760
If working here feels so suffocating,

149
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,760
just come live with me...

150
00:10:34,519 --> 00:10:37,200
instead of crying like a baby like this.

151
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:40,400
Go live with me. I can take care of you.

152
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:42,200
Are you crazy?

153
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:44,680
I'm serious.

154
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:48,160
I may look like this, but I'm rich.

155
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:52,162
I can easily afford to take care of you.

156
00:10:52,162 --> 00:10:53,267
Hey,

157
00:10:53,267 --> 00:10:55,252
I'm not some pet

158
00:10:55,252 --> 00:10:58,253
you can just adopt whenever you want.

159
00:10:58,253 --> 00:11:01,170
I have my own family and responsibilities.

160
00:11:01,170 --> 00:11:03,440
I don't have time to be your toy.

161
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:05,760
I really want to help you.

162
00:11:08,124 --> 00:11:10,474
I don't see you as a toy.

163
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:14,640
If that's the case, thank you so much.

164
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:16,520
But trust me,

165
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:19,360
someone like me is not good enough for you.

166
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:21,440
Why do you put yourself down?

167
00:11:23,936 --> 00:11:25,880
Others might not know this,

168
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:27,760
but I know a woman like you

169
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:30,080
is so much better than those rich people.

170
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:33,860
Like Nana, who is always stepping on others.

171
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:39,243
You didn't do anything wrong, Ran.

172
00:11:39,243 --> 00:11:42,378
Today, you are just fighting for others.

173
00:11:42,378 --> 00:11:44,490
Also,

174
00:11:44,490 --> 00:11:47,521
I really admire you.

175
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:51,240
But my family isn't "others."

176
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:55,160
That's right.

177
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:57,640
So... what are you gonna do now?

178
00:11:57,640 --> 00:12:00,080
If you want to keep fighting here,

179
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:04,799
just know that I'm on your side.

180
00:12:04,799 --> 00:12:08,102
But if you ever change your mind, then...

181
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:10,440
come stay with me. I'll take care of you,

182
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,880
okay?

183
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:13,400
Deal?

184
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:16,320
Do we have a deal?

185
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:21,640
I can't accept this deal.

186
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,960
Still...

187
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:28,240
thank you so much, Sam, for wanting to help.

188
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,800
Okay.

189
00:12:38,695 --> 00:12:41,536
I'm glad you're smiling.

190
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:05,640
I won't lose this time.

191
00:13:14,948 --> 00:13:19,320
She just got here, and now she got fired.

192
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:22,936
Shouldn't have accepted those little bribes.

193
00:13:22,936 --> 00:13:25,040
Right? What a shame.

194
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:26,480
Wrong move.

195
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:28,205
It should've been me.

196
00:13:28,205 --> 00:13:31,360
I want some bribes for myself too.

197
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:33,400
Just kidding.

198
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:35,200
You must be a stand-up comedian.

199
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:37,534
Oh, Mr. Alex.

200
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:41,080
Mr. Alex,

201
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:46,040
is there a way for us
to hold the instigator accountable?

202
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:47,800
That's difficult.

203
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,480
Even though we all know who it is,

204
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:51,440
but we have to let Yai handle this.

205
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:53,360
But let this be an example

206
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:56,762
of what happens when you
sell your professional integrity

207
00:13:56,762 --> 00:13:58,482
for dirty money.

208
00:14:00,177 --> 00:14:01,925
Remember that.

209
00:14:06,333 --> 00:14:07,920
Lek.

210
00:14:10,052 --> 00:14:11,400
Oh!

211
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,240
Nana, are you still here?

212
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,920
I am.

213
00:14:16,654 --> 00:14:20,619
I was waiting to ask you if you realized

214
00:14:20,619 --> 00:14:23,800
that what you did humiliated me.

215
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:26,080
I wasn't the one who humiliated you.

216
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,959
You did that to yourself.

217
00:14:27,959 --> 00:14:30,600
You like to accuse people,
and everyone knows that.

218
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:33,206
If you know nothing, keep your mouth shut.

219
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:38,840
I came to warn you since you're Yai's brother.

220
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:40,880
Why would you let her live with you?

221
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:43,360
She was always seducing Yai since back then.

222
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,480
Are you talking about yourself?

223
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:46,833
Lek.

224
00:14:46,833 --> 00:14:48,280
If you're done, I'm going now.

225
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:50,590
I'm not done!

226
00:14:50,590 --> 00:14:52,800
Are you not done threatening me?

227
00:14:53,977 --> 00:14:56,360
You're funny, really.

228
00:14:56,360 --> 00:15:00,920
What do you like so much
about your brother's ex-girlfriend?

229
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:03,560
For you to help her this much,

230
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:05,920
how many times have you slept with her?

231
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:09,800
Please show some respect.

232
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:13,600
Ran and I have never done what you said.

233
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:19,050
I respect Ran as a sister,
and I'll never steal someone Yai loves.

234
00:15:19,873 --> 00:15:22,280
You'll never steal someone Yai loves?

235
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:25,120
When a man and a woman are alone in a room,

236
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:27,360
if they're not having sex,

237
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,480
what else would they do?

238
00:15:30,287 --> 00:15:32,860
I thought you'd be smarter, Lek.

239
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:35,040
Never thought you'd fall for an ordinary woman.

240
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:37,080
Nana.

241
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:39,760
Have you ever asked yourself

242
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:42,200
if the reason you're doing this

243
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:45,680
is because you don't want people
to be fooled by Ran,

244
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:47,920
or because you just hate her?

245
00:15:49,277 --> 00:15:53,680
I think instead of spending your time
slandering people like this,

246
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:55,960
you should use it to better yourself.

247
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:58,160
Keep running your mouth while you can, Lek.

248
00:15:58,160 --> 00:15:59,760
I'll deal with you later. Just you wait.

249
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:03,360
I'm not gonna wait for you.
I don't know you like that.

250
00:16:05,409 --> 00:16:07,840
Stupid, obnoxious asshole.

251
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:40,244
Is she not back yet?

252
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:48,800
Whoa!

253
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:49,974
Ran...

254
00:16:49,974 --> 00:16:53,000
When did you come back?

255
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,320
I've been here for a while, Mr. Alex.

256
00:16:58,287 --> 00:17:00,920
- Ran...
- Don't!

257
00:17:01,873 --> 00:17:05,080
Do you understand
how it feels to be fooled now?

258
00:17:13,551 --> 00:17:17,120
I've been wondering
how a security guard could be like this.

259
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:19,400
It's clear now.

260
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,800
I had no ill intentions.

261
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:24,760
I didn't tell you that I'm Lek,
Yai's younger brother,

262
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:26,520
because I meant well.

263
00:17:28,012 --> 00:17:29,104
Ran.

264
00:17:29,104 --> 00:17:30,160
Stop, Mr. Lek.

265
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:31,520
What are you doing?

266
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,350
- Mr. Lek.
- No!

267
00:17:33,350 --> 00:17:35,400
- Mr. Lek!
- No!

268
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,840
- Mr. Lek!
- No!

269
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:39,440
This is a bra!

270
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:40,920
Whoa!

271
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:42,654
I'm sorry.

272
00:17:45,449 --> 00:17:48,280
Why are you packing these things?

273
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:50,607
You're Yai's younger brother.

274
00:17:50,607 --> 00:17:53,172
If I stay here, it'll only cause more trouble.

275
00:17:53,172 --> 00:17:54,597
Don't say that.

276
00:17:54,597 --> 00:17:56,702
I was the one who invited you to live here,

277
00:17:56,702 --> 00:17:58,427
which means you can stay here.

278
00:17:58,427 --> 00:18:00,200
And I mean that sincerely.

279
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:02,260
I've never thought of you romantically.

280
00:18:02,260 --> 00:18:06,371
But if you're uncomfortable, I'll leave.

281
00:18:06,371 --> 00:18:08,880
I know you don't think of me like that.

282
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:11,400
But how can you be the one leaving?

283
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:13,920
If you don't want to live with me anymore,

284
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:15,560
I'll leave.

285
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:17,740
But you can't leave.

286
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:20,320
- Mr. Lek.
- No.

287
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:22,088
Call me properly.

288
00:18:23,134 --> 00:18:24,600
Lek.

289
00:18:26,837 --> 00:18:30,000
Thank you for being so kind to me.

290
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,440
But I don't want the fact that we share a room

291
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:35,552
to become an issue that can cause you trouble

292
00:18:35,552 --> 00:18:37,845
or arguments with your own brother.

293
00:18:37,845 --> 00:18:40,926
But I was the one
who said I wanted to help you.

294
00:18:40,926 --> 00:18:42,640
You've helped me,

295
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:45,680
and you've helped me
more than anyone else I've met.

296
00:18:46,723 --> 00:18:49,520
But no matter what,
I'm still going to leave today.

297
00:18:56,317 --> 00:19:00,240
No matter what I do, you'll still leave, right?

298
00:19:10,957 --> 00:19:15,057
Then, can I at least find you a new room?

299
00:19:16,692 --> 00:19:19,440
You can't stop me from helping you.

300
00:19:20,364 --> 00:19:21,848
It's not happening.

301
00:19:26,371 --> 00:19:27,856
Thank you.

302
00:19:31,442 --> 00:19:35,120
But... the fact that you're gay.

303
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:37,040
Is it true?

304
00:19:38,457 --> 00:19:40,280
Oh.

305
00:19:41,309 --> 00:19:45,680
About that, Ran... I'm sorry.

306
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:47,520
Who taught you to be a liar?

307
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:49,560
- How did you turn out like this?
- Ran, I'm sorry.

308
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:51,160
- I'm going to hit you!
- Ran, I'm sorry!

309
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:52,760
- Let me hit you, Lek!
- Ran! Ow!

310
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:53,740
Ran!

311
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:55,897
- Lek! Why did you lie to me?
- Ran! Ouch!

312
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:59,080
- How did you turn out like this?
- Ran!

313
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:01,940
- How could you lie to me?
- I'm sorry!

314
00:20:40,767 --> 00:20:43,280
Well done, Daran.

315
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:45,520
Now you've got both Lek and Sam.

316
00:21:01,668 --> 00:21:03,400
Fight!

317
00:21:10,718 --> 00:21:12,282
Get in the car.

318
00:21:15,718 --> 00:21:18,111
I told you to get in.

319
00:21:18,111 --> 00:21:20,240
No, sir.

320
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:22,480
I said, "Get in the car."

321
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:24,960
I can walk on my own.

322
00:21:28,450 --> 00:21:30,120
This is the last time.

323
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:31,720
Get in the car.

324
00:22:02,739 --> 00:22:04,009
What do you want?

325
00:22:04,009 --> 00:22:06,640
I should be the one asking you that.

326
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:08,960
Why are you sharing a room with Lek?

327
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:12,104
It's a personal matter, sir.

328
00:22:12,104 --> 00:22:13,960
Are you trying to seduce Lek?

329
00:22:15,174 --> 00:22:16,480
And Sam, too.

330
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:18,160
Aren't you two in love?

331
00:22:19,768 --> 00:22:22,160
- That is also a personal matter.
- It's not.

332
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:25,968
You share a room with my brother
and are so close to Sam.

333
00:22:25,968 --> 00:22:27,720
Isn't that going too far?

334
00:22:29,096 --> 00:22:31,080
No, it's not.

335
00:22:31,080 --> 00:22:32,920
I don't want to talk.

336
00:22:35,299 --> 00:22:37,160
Open it. I'm leaving.

337
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:39,375
I'm warning you.

338
00:22:39,375 --> 00:22:43,748
Don't you think
I'll ever let Lek or Sam date you.

339
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:47,786
I don't want them to make the same mistake.

340
00:23:04,982 --> 00:23:07,052
This is your job.

341
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:09,560
Move everything here to the wall over there.

342
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:11,040
Finish this before noon.

343
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:12,770
Huh? Noon?

344
00:23:12,770 --> 00:23:14,553
Yes.

345
00:23:14,553 --> 00:23:16,123
Noon.

346
00:23:16,123 --> 00:23:18,520
They'll put new stuff here tomorrow.

347
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:20,640
Is this an actual job or just a prank?

348
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,520
Are you going to do it?

349
00:23:24,597 --> 00:23:26,200
I am, sir.

350
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:30,240
Don't break anything.

351
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:33,280
Otherwise, you'll have to pay for it.

352
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:34,920
Yes, sir.

353
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:46,320
I'm done, sir.

354
00:24:47,103 --> 00:24:48,800
There's a change.

355
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:51,354
We'll have to move to another studio.

356
00:24:51,354 --> 00:24:53,895
Move them outside.

357
00:24:53,895 --> 00:24:56,000
I just finished moving them, though.

358
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:58,240
If you can't do it, just quit.

359
00:25:39,447 --> 00:25:41,420
They're here. Where do you want me to move?

360
00:25:41,420 --> 00:25:43,663
It's canceled. The truck's not here.

361
00:25:43,663 --> 00:25:45,220
Move them back to their place.

362
00:25:45,220 --> 00:25:46,600
What did you say?

363
00:25:46,600 --> 00:25:47,867
I'll say it once.

364
00:25:47,867 --> 00:25:50,528
If you can't do it, just quit.

365
00:26:09,120 --> 00:26:10,440
[Loy Krathong Festival]
[2013]

366
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:11,800
<i>Yai.</i>

367
00:26:20,560 --> 00:26:21,920
<i>Yai...</i>

368
00:26:21,920 --> 00:26:24,374
<i>Drink carefully.</i>

369
00:26:24,374 --> 00:26:26,160
<i>Thank you for helping me.</i>

370
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:28,296
<i>So refreshing.</i>

371
00:26:28,296 --> 00:26:29,680
<i>But...</i>

372
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:31,160
<i>Is this just water?</i>

373
00:26:31,160 --> 00:26:33,480
<i>It's water.</i>

374
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:35,990
<i>Really? Well...</i>

375
00:26:35,990 --> 00:26:37,717
<i>Why is it so sweet?</i>

376
00:26:37,717 --> 00:26:39,318
<i>Or is it because...</i>

377
00:26:39,318 --> 00:26:42,028
<i>the one who got it for me is also sweet?</i>

378
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:46,160
<i>- Yai!
- Ran...</i>

379
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:47,600
<i>Why did you push me?</i>

380
00:26:47,600 --> 00:26:49,880
<i>It's nothing.</i>

381
00:27:11,601 --> 00:27:13,360
Drink carefully.

382
00:27:16,015 --> 00:27:17,560
Thank you.

383
00:27:18,343 --> 00:27:21,169
It's done... for the third time.

384
00:27:21,169 --> 00:27:23,320
Do you want me to move them to Mars next?

385
00:27:23,320 --> 00:27:25,040
Watch your tone.

386
00:27:25,040 --> 00:27:27,040
Well, I'm just a mere security guard.

387
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:29,460
You just have to do your job.

388
00:27:30,659 --> 00:27:33,520
You had no problem
moving things into a man's room.

389
00:27:35,229 --> 00:27:37,200
This again?

390
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:38,500
I'll say it again.

391
00:27:38,500 --> 00:27:41,000
Lek and I had nothing going on.

392
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:42,705
We're just friends.

393
00:27:42,705 --> 00:27:44,960
Also, I've moved out of his room.

394
00:27:44,960 --> 00:27:49,240
Don't worry
that I'll drag your brother down with me.

395
00:27:58,367 --> 00:28:00,226
Are you satisfied now?

396
00:28:00,226 --> 00:28:01,960
Come on.

397
00:28:01,960 --> 00:28:04,520
Just order me around or bully me all you want.

398
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:06,927
You have the power to do that.

399
00:28:06,927 --> 00:28:08,240
I'm just an evil woman.

400
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:10,107
Don't challenge me.

401
00:28:10,107 --> 00:28:13,074
And don't play the victim like you did nothing.

402
00:28:14,040 --> 00:28:17,960
Back then,
everything I did was for a woman like you.

403
00:28:20,492 --> 00:28:22,640
It was even worse than this.

404
00:28:25,305 --> 00:28:26,720
Don't mention the past.

405
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:28,320
I will.

406
00:28:34,586 --> 00:28:39,840
Wasn't it all because of you
that we ended up like this?

407
00:30:00,320 --> 00:30:02,440
[2026]

408
00:30:02,440 --> 00:30:05,360
Yai, do you want a picture with Ran?
[2013]

409
00:30:05,360 --> 00:30:06,660
Yeah, stand next to her.

410
00:30:06,660 --> 00:30:08,180
Yeah!

411
00:30:08,180 --> 00:30:11,340
Okay, three, two, one!

412
00:30:13,701 --> 00:30:15,640
You're so beautiful.

413
00:30:21,261 --> 00:30:23,480
Yai, here's the camera.

414
00:30:24,375 --> 00:30:27,720
How can anyone be so cute when mad,
yet so damn fierce?

415
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:29,680
And this is an important moment

416
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:32,274
when our Noppamas Queens will take the stage.

417
00:30:32,274 --> 00:30:36,626
Whoever you like,
or are secretly rooting for...

418
00:30:36,626 --> 00:30:38,750
Just how beautiful they'll be...

419
00:30:38,750 --> 00:30:40,200
you'll have to wait and see.

420
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:43,180
Our first contestant is...

421
00:30:43,180 --> 00:30:44,680
Yai!

422
00:30:45,852 --> 00:30:47,840
Someone put a glass shard in Ran's shoe.

423
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:49,040
The cut is very deep.

424
00:30:49,040 --> 00:30:51,160
Nilapia is taking her to the hospital.

425
00:30:55,430 --> 00:30:57,680
Anyway, be careful.

426
00:30:57,680 --> 00:31:01,280
No one can take care of us better than we can.

427
00:31:01,280 --> 00:31:03,407
Yes, Miss.

428
00:31:03,407 --> 00:31:05,000
I'll do it.

429
00:31:07,014 --> 00:31:09,360
I will take care of Ran.

430
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:12,818
I've taken care of the medical expense.

431
00:31:12,818 --> 00:31:16,185
I'll also be the one to take Ran home, Miss.

432
00:31:16,185 --> 00:31:18,779
I'll inform Daran's parents about this, then.

433
00:31:18,779 --> 00:31:20,621
Yes. Thank you, Miss.

434
00:31:21,720 --> 00:31:22,660
Ran!

435
00:31:22,660 --> 00:31:23,880
Oh, no.

436
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:26,160
Ran, how are you? Does it hurt?

437
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:28,680
I was about to head to the hospital.

438
00:31:28,680 --> 00:31:30,520
I'm fine, Mom.

439
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:31,680
How are you, dear?

440
00:31:31,680 --> 00:31:33,640
What did they say? Was the wound deep?

441
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:35,251
Can you still do taekwondo?

442
00:31:35,251 --> 00:31:36,800
Don't worry, Dad.

443
00:31:36,800 --> 00:31:40,160
They said once I'm better,
I'll be able to play sports like before.

444
00:31:46,568 --> 00:31:48,520
Hello, sir. Hello, ma'am.

445
00:31:48,520 --> 00:31:50,040
I'm Yai,

446
00:31:50,040 --> 00:31:52,280
Daran's classmate.

447
00:31:53,675 --> 00:31:55,421
Why are you here?

448
00:31:55,421 --> 00:31:56,520
I...

449
00:31:56,520 --> 00:31:58,679
Yai was the one who took me to the hospital.

450
00:31:58,679 --> 00:31:59,840
That's right, Dad.

451
00:31:59,840 --> 00:32:02,120
Yai took care of everything for us.

452
00:32:02,120 --> 00:32:04,440
We were so nervous we didn't know what to do.

453
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:08,141
He also volunteered to give Ran a ride home.

454
00:32:08,141 --> 00:32:11,581
Did you have to walk her in like that?

455
00:32:12,210 --> 00:32:13,840
Honey.

456
00:32:14,891 --> 00:32:17,218
Thank you.

457
00:32:17,218 --> 00:32:18,520
Yes.

458
00:32:18,520 --> 00:32:21,160
Thank you for taking care of this.

459
00:32:21,160 --> 00:32:23,120
Get some rest, Ran.

460
00:32:23,120 --> 00:32:25,800
Are you going to sleep here with Ran?
It's late now.

461
00:32:25,800 --> 00:32:28,200
Yes, Dad. I'll sleep here.

462
00:32:29,194 --> 00:32:31,554
Should you go home? It's late now.

463
00:32:31,554 --> 00:32:32,740
Dad.

464
00:32:32,740 --> 00:32:38,421
For now, can I ask you to let Yai
drive Ran to and from school?

465
00:32:38,421 --> 00:32:39,840
Her feet hurt.

466
00:32:39,840 --> 00:32:42,360
Taking the bus will be hard for her.

467
00:32:42,360 --> 00:32:45,360
Her wound might take longer to heal, too.

468
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:47,360
Really.

469
00:32:47,360 --> 00:32:49,560
Can I trust you?

470
00:32:50,496 --> 00:32:51,480
Yes.

471
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:53,280
Take care of Ran, then.

472
00:32:53,280 --> 00:32:57,160
But next time, just drop her off.

473
00:32:57,160 --> 00:32:58,960
You don't need to walk her in.

474
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:01,600
Yes.

475
00:33:02,280 --> 00:33:03,960
Then goodbye, sir.

476
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:05,680
- Goodbye.
- Yes.

477
00:33:08,960 --> 00:33:11,440
Ran, I'm leaving now.

478
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:13,120
Get well soon.

479
00:33:20,582 --> 00:33:22,320
Goodbye, Dad.

480
00:33:52,369 --> 00:33:55,198
- Can you take me to Ran?
- Okay.

481
00:33:57,658 --> 00:34:00,360
Ran, your boyfriend's here.

482
00:34:00,360 --> 00:34:01,520
You rascal!

483
00:34:01,520 --> 00:34:03,940
Do you know what a boyfriend is, hm?

484
00:34:04,673 --> 00:34:05,800
Danai!

485
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:07,280
You got it all over your lips.

486
00:34:07,280 --> 00:34:08,520
They're all messy now.

487
00:34:08,520 --> 00:34:12,480
Next time, if a thief asks to come in,
how would I know?

488
00:34:13,282 --> 00:34:15,880
Your brother told me
your dad isn't home, right?

489
00:34:16,954 --> 00:34:20,071
Did you bribe my brother with desserts?

490
00:34:20,071 --> 00:34:21,320
Your brother's adorable.

491
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:23,815
Don't scold him. What's his name?

492
00:34:23,815 --> 00:34:25,932
He's Danai.

493
00:34:25,932 --> 00:34:28,200
How did you get here?

494
00:34:28,200 --> 00:34:30,200
I promised I'd come to see you.

495
00:34:30,200 --> 00:34:32,760
What about you? Does it hurt a lot?

496
00:34:33,691 --> 00:34:36,225
Ran, does it still hurt?

497
00:34:36,225 --> 00:34:38,090
It hurts less today.

498
00:34:38,090 --> 00:34:40,000
When will you get better?

499
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:41,120
I don't know.

500
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:42,680
But I'll get better soon.

501
00:34:42,680 --> 00:34:45,880
If you cast a spell on me,
it might get better even sooner.

502
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:48,360
- Oh.
- Watch your head.

503
00:34:48,360 --> 00:34:49,680
Poof!

504
00:34:51,626 --> 00:34:53,231
Is it better now?

505
00:34:53,231 --> 00:34:56,040
It is. Good job, Danai.

506
00:34:58,147 --> 00:35:00,240
Come on, I'll dress the wound.

507
00:35:00,240 --> 00:35:01,680
Don't.

508
00:35:01,680 --> 00:35:04,480
Don't be stubborn. Move your leg here.

509
00:35:07,951 --> 00:35:10,720
Do you think I'd only like it
when you're standing?

510
00:35:10,720 --> 00:35:13,760
Even with a bad leg, I'd still like you.

511
00:35:13,760 --> 00:35:15,480
Look at you.

512
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:17,606
Isn't that embarrassing, Yai?

513
00:35:17,606 --> 00:35:21,192
If saying that means you'll
let me dress your wound every day,

514
00:35:21,192 --> 00:35:22,933
I'm not embarrassed.

515
00:35:27,527 --> 00:35:30,720
But it'd be best if you weren't wounded at all.

516
00:35:33,200 --> 00:35:34,753
I'll protect you.

517
00:35:34,753 --> 00:35:36,662
I won't let you get hurt anymore.

518
00:36:07,917 --> 00:36:09,454
Puff!

519
00:36:13,378 --> 00:36:14,960
There is no evidence.

520
00:36:14,960 --> 00:36:16,120
Why should we be scared?

521
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:18,480
But I'm scared!

522
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:20,640
Can you stop acting suspicious?

523
00:36:20,640 --> 00:36:22,400
Just act normal.

524
00:36:22,400 --> 00:36:23,720
If there's any trouble,

525
00:36:23,720 --> 00:36:25,680
Nana's father would take care of it for us.

526
00:36:25,680 --> 00:36:28,370
His newspaper company is huge.

527
00:36:28,370 --> 00:36:32,600
The daughter of a mere soy milk vendor
versus me,

528
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:34,720
who do you think will win?

529
00:36:46,402 --> 00:36:49,207
I don't like sharing a bathroom with anyone.

530
00:36:57,433 --> 00:36:59,243
Why did you scream?

531
00:37:07,479 --> 00:37:08,920
Open the door!

532
00:37:08,920 --> 00:37:10,560
Open the door!

533
00:37:10,560 --> 00:37:12,560
I told you to open it!

534
00:37:14,198 --> 00:37:15,720
Open the door!

535
00:37:15,720 --> 00:37:17,700
I told you to open the door!

536
00:37:17,700 --> 00:37:19,040
Open the door!

537
00:37:19,040 --> 00:37:21,200
It won't open!

538
00:37:22,280 --> 00:37:24,600
Get off me!

539
00:37:25,320 --> 00:37:26,680
Open the door!

540
00:37:26,680 --> 00:37:28,280
Nana!

541
00:37:31,129 --> 00:37:32,555
Hey!

542
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:37,440
Yai!

543
00:37:37,440 --> 00:37:40,920
- Ran.
- Are you okay, Yai?

544
00:37:40,920 --> 00:37:43,840
You said you'd protect me
from getting hurt again.

545
00:37:43,840 --> 00:37:45,400
Will you be able to do that?

546
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:49,040
You yelped when I kicked you just now.

547
00:37:49,620 --> 00:37:50,640
You're too tough.

548
00:37:50,640 --> 00:37:52,981
Do you still like me if I'm so tough?

549
00:37:52,981 --> 00:37:54,426
I don't anymore.

550
00:37:54,426 --> 00:37:56,360
Oh?

551
00:37:56,360 --> 00:37:58,659
I stopped liking you long ago.

552
00:37:59,512 --> 00:38:01,649
Because I love you instead.

553
00:38:04,520 --> 00:38:08,801
So, when can we tell your parents we're dating?

554
00:38:08,801 --> 00:38:11,920
Aren't you scared my dad might kill you?

555
00:38:13,028 --> 00:38:14,560
Why would I be?

556
00:38:14,560 --> 00:38:18,560
I'm so good-looking,
and my status is even better.

557
00:38:18,560 --> 00:38:20,920
A future television station executive.

558
00:38:21,621 --> 00:38:23,320
How can he not like me?

559
00:38:29,320 --> 00:38:31,394
That's exactly...

560
00:38:31,394 --> 00:38:33,189
what I'm worried about.

561
00:38:34,035 --> 00:38:35,220
Why?

562
00:38:35,220 --> 00:38:39,960
Someone as perfect as you dating me...

563
00:38:52,004 --> 00:38:53,926
I love you.

564
00:38:53,926 --> 00:38:57,640
I don't care about the differences between us.

565
00:38:57,640 --> 00:39:01,500
All that matters is how we feel.

566
00:39:01,500 --> 00:39:03,221
Got it?

567
00:39:14,731 --> 00:39:18,400
What are you thinking about,
just standing there smiling?

568
00:39:19,960 --> 00:39:21,640
Dad...

569
00:39:22,585 --> 00:39:27,840
If I love someone, would you be okay with that?

570
00:39:29,466 --> 00:39:33,720
If you love someone, I'll love him too.

571
00:39:34,885 --> 00:39:36,536
Thank you, Dad.

572
00:39:36,536 --> 00:39:38,040
It's okay to be in love.

573
00:39:38,040 --> 00:39:42,080
I won't stop you, because it's only natural.

574
00:39:42,080 --> 00:39:43,680
Also, I think

575
00:39:43,680 --> 00:39:47,360
you must've thought it through
and can take care of yourself.

576
00:39:48,500 --> 00:39:50,609
But I'll only ask you

577
00:39:50,609 --> 00:39:54,440
to never forget your duties
and responsibilities.

578
00:39:55,242 --> 00:39:59,980
Yes, Dad. I'll never disappoint you.

579
00:40:02,594 --> 00:40:03,840
Come here.

580
00:40:03,840 --> 00:40:05,720
Oh, you're really all grown up.

581
00:40:05,720 --> 00:40:07,160
Whoa...

582
00:40:08,284 --> 00:40:11,343
I've watched you grow up,
and now you're in love.

583
00:40:23,627 --> 00:40:24,520
Kick!

584
00:40:24,520 --> 00:40:25,920
Kick...

585
00:40:26,643 --> 00:40:28,600
You are here again?

586
00:40:28,600 --> 00:40:31,468
Yes. Hello.

587
00:40:32,720 --> 00:40:35,198
Can I really trust you?

588
00:40:35,198 --> 00:40:36,640
Of course.

589
00:40:38,362 --> 00:40:40,360
Be patient, dear!

590
00:40:41,560 --> 00:40:43,120
Be patient!

591
00:40:44,360 --> 00:40:47,540
- It's okay.
- It's okay, Ran.

592
00:40:51,440 --> 00:40:53,720
- Yay!
- Yay!

593
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:55,640
You won, Ran!

594
00:40:57,333 --> 00:40:59,360
Yay!

595
00:41:00,200 --> 00:41:02,290
- Yay!
- Sir.

596
00:41:02,290 --> 00:41:05,947
- Yes?
- May I have your permission to date Ran?

597
00:41:16,517 --> 00:41:18,312
Thank you...

598
00:41:19,480 --> 00:41:23,560
for being brave enough to say it
and being a man about it.

599
00:41:23,560 --> 00:41:25,156
But...

600
00:41:26,870 --> 00:41:28,960
can I really trust you?

601
00:41:30,424 --> 00:41:31,921
Of course.

602
00:41:36,609 --> 00:41:38,840
Good job, Ran.

603
00:41:38,840 --> 00:41:41,340
Enough, enough. That's too much.

604
00:41:41,340 --> 00:41:42,780
- Okay.
- Step back.

605
00:41:45,744 --> 00:41:46,760
Good job.

606
00:41:46,760 --> 00:41:47,901
- Thank you.
- Good job.

607
00:41:47,901 --> 00:41:49,800
Congratulations. That's my girl.

608
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:51,445
Excellent.

609
00:41:52,732 --> 00:41:53,960
- I'm going now.
- Bye-bye.

610
00:41:53,960 --> 00:41:56,320
- Bye-bye!
- Bye.

611
00:41:58,511 --> 00:41:59,760
Ooh!

612
00:41:59,760 --> 00:42:01,240
Yai.

613
00:42:01,240 --> 00:42:03,520
Did you carry stones to school?

614
00:42:08,729 --> 00:42:10,560
Yai's house is freaking huge!

615
00:42:10,560 --> 00:42:11,960
The atmosphere is so nice.

616
00:42:11,960 --> 00:42:15,856
Thank you, Yai,
for the high school graduation party!

617
00:42:17,443 --> 00:42:19,981
Three, two, one!

618
00:42:20,912 --> 00:42:22,400
- Yeah! That's great.
- Oh!

619
00:42:22,400 --> 00:42:23,720
- Whoa!
- Over there!

620
00:42:23,720 --> 00:42:24,960
Yeah, nice!

621
00:42:24,960 --> 00:42:26,560
Oh, hey!

622
00:42:28,357 --> 00:42:31,020
A, E, I, O, U!

623
00:42:32,466 --> 00:42:34,800
A, E, I, O, U!

624
00:42:38,124 --> 00:42:39,300
[Graduated!]

625
00:42:39,300 --> 00:42:40,320
[See you again]

626
00:42:40,320 --> 00:42:41,920
[Wish you luck]

627
00:42:43,757 --> 00:42:46,480
[Pretty girl]

628
00:42:47,452 --> 00:42:49,220
[Daran]

629
00:42:51,920 --> 00:42:54,840
- Chirp, chirp!
- Hey.

630
00:42:54,840 --> 00:42:55,840
There are whiskers.

631
00:42:55,840 --> 00:42:57,800
[Tiger]

632
00:43:00,720 --> 00:43:02,080
Lion?
[Lion]

633
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:03,920
- Yeah!
- Is it?

634
00:43:04,880 --> 00:43:06,320
Yeah!

635
00:43:06,320 --> 00:43:10,440
<i>♪ If you're a mountain, then I'll be a forest ♪</i>

636
00:43:10,440 --> 00:43:14,320
<i>♪ Embracing you to keep you warm in my chest ♪</i>

637
00:43:14,320 --> 00:43:18,440
<i>♪ If you're the sky, then I'll be the clouds ♪</i>

638
00:43:18,440 --> 00:43:22,720
<i>♪ Embracing you to keep you company ♪</i>

639
00:43:24,280 --> 00:43:25,320
Cheers!

640
00:43:25,320 --> 00:43:26,994
Cheers.

641
00:43:39,998 --> 00:43:41,767
You might get sick.

642
00:43:52,120 --> 00:43:54,029
Are you not cold?

643
00:43:54,029 --> 00:43:55,929
Why don't we share it?

644
00:44:22,074 --> 00:44:24,502
What should I do with these guys?

645
00:44:45,228 --> 00:44:48,176
Chickens are roasted...

646
00:44:53,720 --> 00:44:55,251
Yai...

647
00:44:55,251 --> 00:44:56,714
How are they?

648
00:44:56,714 --> 00:44:58,696
They're all out cold.

649
00:44:58,696 --> 00:45:00,200
You can take a shower upstairs.

650
00:45:00,200 --> 00:45:01,660
There's a room available.

651
00:45:01,660 --> 00:45:03,640
It belongs to my father and Grandma.

652
00:45:03,640 --> 00:45:05,200
Would that be okay?

653
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:06,280
It's fine.

654
00:45:06,280 --> 00:45:08,340
I own the house now.

655
00:45:38,569 --> 00:45:40,955
I've done this to Grandma before.

656
00:45:41,960 --> 00:45:45,200
I didn't even ask anything.

657
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:47,160
I can see it in your eyes.

658
00:45:59,609 --> 00:46:01,325
Thank you.

659
00:46:32,906 --> 00:46:34,560
So beautiful.

660
00:46:35,480 --> 00:46:37,278
Do you like stargazing?

661
00:46:37,278 --> 00:46:39,280
I never knew that.

662
00:46:42,237 --> 00:46:45,520
When my father was alive,
he liked to take me here.

663
00:46:46,432 --> 00:46:48,360
You miss your father, right?

664
00:46:51,588 --> 00:46:53,800
Now, I miss you more.

665
00:46:55,252 --> 00:46:56,940
I'm right here.

666
00:46:56,940 --> 00:46:58,920
Why would you miss me?

667
00:47:00,937 --> 00:47:04,360
When I go away to study,
we'll have to be apart.

668
00:47:06,015 --> 00:47:07,640
That's true.

669
00:47:08,297 --> 00:47:11,360
I know it's for your future,

670
00:47:11,360 --> 00:47:15,458
but just thinking about us being apart

671
00:47:15,458 --> 00:47:17,880
makes me feel so lonely, I can't explain it.

672
00:47:23,252 --> 00:47:27,240
Yai, will I still be with you in the future?

673
00:47:27,240 --> 00:47:33,233
Soon, we'll get married
and build a family together.

674
00:47:34,452 --> 00:47:36,240
Please wait for me.

675
00:47:37,813 --> 00:47:40,000
I'll wait for you, Yai.

676
00:48:45,524 --> 00:48:48,456
What we are doing is wrong, Yai.

677
00:48:49,720 --> 00:48:51,520
I love you so much.

678
00:48:55,031 --> 00:48:57,000
I love you, too.

679
00:50:05,667 --> 00:50:07,680
I love you, Yai.

680
00:50:09,550 --> 00:50:11,822
I love you even more.

681
00:50:11,822 --> 00:50:13,760
I love you the most.

682
00:50:15,003 --> 00:50:17,480
I'll only love you forever.

683
00:50:49,563 --> 00:50:52,306
<i>Don't even play games with Sam or Lek.</i>
[Keep going. Don't tell Yai]

684
00:50:52,306 --> 00:50:55,662
<i>I've been thinking who I should fool.</i>

685
00:50:59,200 --> 00:51:01,440
<i>Ran! Ran! Ran!</i>

686
00:51:01,440 --> 00:51:04,480
<i>Do you hate or care about her?</i>

687
00:51:05,821 --> 00:51:07,240
<i>Hang in there until that day.</i>

688
00:51:07,240 --> 00:51:11,160
<i>I'll make sure you and
our child live comfortably and happily.</i>

689
00:51:15,727 --> 00:51:19,240
<i>I don't want you to
go through this to take care of me.</i>
